ipt (`probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:2997` self-labels `\"emission_granularity\": \"per arm user-step transmission census\"`) and to per-configuration counters in the batch path. Implemented disposition otherwise matches the confirmation document.\n  \n  ---\n  \n  ## (a) Three distinct objects + emission — **LANDED (with a scope caveat)**\n  \n  - Distinct fields, no aliasing: `src/mcrl/physics_v025/architectures.py:193-195` (`m_target: ACMMode|None`, `m_tx: ACMMode|None`, `realised_outcome: ACMRealisedOutcome|None`), plus `nominal_sinr` / `margin_predicted_sinr` at `:196-197`.\n  - `ACMRealisedOutcome` is a separate frozen type: `src/mcrl/physics_v025/acm.py:30-36`.\n  - Single construction site: `architectures.py:480-510`. `m_target` is passed in from `_rate_targets` (`:729-747`), `m_tx` is computed independently at `:480`, `realised_outcome` at `:484`. Three separate objects, no shared reference.\n  - Emission (scalar/receipt): `probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:1531-1541` builds `mode_counts` (credited), `target_counts`, `transmitted_counts`, `decode_successes/failures`; serialised at `:2990-2998` as `acm_causal_objects.{m_target_counts, m_tx_counts, realised_outcome.{decoded,outage}}`.\n  - Emission (batch): `batch.py:48-50` fields `target_mode_counts / transmitted_mode_counts / realised_decode_successes`, filled at `:453-475`.\n  \n  **Caveats.** (1) `m_target` is `None` for architectures `b`, `a-γ`, `a′-γ` — `_transmissions` is called without `m_target_values` at `architectures.py:576-578`, `:629-633`, `:699-703`. Only `a-r` (`:833`) and `a′-r` (`:936`) carry all three. Defensible (only rate-target arms have a target mode), but \"all three per user-step\" is not universal. (2) Nothing in `src/` writes a per-user-step row; only aggregate counts survive into receipts.\n  \n  ## (b) `m_tx` from the causal nominal view — **LANDED. No leakage found.**\n  \n  Full input trace of `select_transmitted_mode(nominal_sinr, quantile)` (`architectures.py:480`):\n  \n  1. `nominal_sinr = nominal_sinr_values[row]`, from `architectures.py:462-463`:\n     `nominal_sinr_values = power * nominal_direct / (noise + nominal_coupling @ power)`.\n  2. `nominal_direct` ← `geometry.gains(\"nominal\")` at every call site (`:556`, `:629-631`, `:699-701`, `:783`, `:874-876`). `gains(\"nominal\")` returns `link.nominal_gain` only (`architectures.py:106-107`) — the realised branch is `:121-126` and is never taken for this argument.\n  3. `nominal_coupling` ← `_masked_coupling(..., \"nominal\")` at `:557`, `:602`, `:666`, `:784`, `:877`. The realised coupling is a *separate* variable (`field_coupling`) used only for `actual_sinr`.\n  4. `power` ← `_solve_power(nominal_direct, nominal_coupling, ...)` at `:604-611`, `:668-675`, `:790-800`, `:883-893`; the solver's update at `architectures.py:430` divides by the nominal `direct`. `FixedRF` uses the constant cap (`:553`). **Power carries no realised gain.**\n  5. `quantile` ← `fading_product_quantile(link.elevation_deg, alpha)` (`:475-479`), which depends only on elevation bin + α (`channel.py:303-307`), not on any draw.\n  \n  `actual_sinr` is computed at `:481-483`, strictly *after* `m_tx` at `:480`, and is not an input to it. `select_transmitted_mode` (`acm.py:73-83`) reads nothing else. Batch mirror: `predicted_sinr = nominal_sinr * quantile` (`batch.py:398-403`), `nominal_sinr` from `direct_nominal` and `nominal_cross` (`:260`, `:284`, `:395-402`); `direct_field`/`field_cross` (`:266-295`) are used only for the realised `sinr` at `:386-390`. Clean.\n  \n  ## (c) Credit rule — **LANDED**\n  \n  - `acm.py:86-98` `decode_transmitted_mode`: `decoded = mode is not None and realised_sinr_linear &gt;= mode.threshold_linear`; credited SE is `0.0` when not decoded, else `mode.spectral_efficiency_bit_per_s_hz`. The mode is `m_tx`, passed in — no re-argmax over realised SINR.\n  - Crediting consumers all read `realised_outcome.credited_spectral_efficiency_bit_per_s_hz`, never `select_mode(realised)`: `resolution.py:126-139`, `adapter.py:175-190`, `architectures.py:288-295`.\n  - Batch: `batch.py:416-419` — `transmitted_threshold = thresholds[mode_index]`; `served = active &amp; has_tx_mode &amp; (sinr &gt;= transmitted_threshold)`; `slot_rate = where(served, efficiencies[mode_index]*BW, 0)`. `threshold(m_target)` (`gamma`, `:118-126`) is used only to set power (`:313`, `:368-373`) and for `boundary_feasible` (`:446`) — never for decode.\n  - `ACMRate.rate_bps` (`acm.py:172-178`) still does realised-argmax `select_mode(sinr)`, but every ACM caller takes the `isinstance(model, ACMRate)` branch that bypasses it (`resolution.py:126`, `adapter.py:175`). It remains a live footgun (still exported, still exercised by `tests/physics_v025/test_constants_acm.py:68-117`), not a live defect.\n  \n  ## (d) Scalar/batch drift — **PARTIAL**\n  \n  Rules are algebraically identical (selection on `nominal×quantile`, first-max-efficiency tie-break, `&gt;=` comparisons, decode against `thresholds[mode_index]`, zero otherwise; `has_tx_mode` guards the `argmax`-returns-0 degenerate case at `batch.py:407-417`). I found **no semantic drift.**\n  \n  The gap is verification: **no test ever exercises the batch path with a fading quantile.** `grep fading_quantile_alpha tests/` returns only scalar-config hits (`test_architectures.py:247`, `test_stage4h_amendments.py:104,128`, `test_integration_matrix.py:198`); every `evaluate_ar_tdm_catalogue` call in tests leaves `fading_quantile_alpha=None`. The one parity test, `tests/physics_v025/test_stage4d_gate.py:655-685`, runs `field=\"nominal\"` with α unset — so `quantile == 1` and `realised == nominal`, and the corrected branch (`batch.py:403-419`) collapses to the old behaviour. The batch causal-ACM implementation is untested under the semantics it was written for, and no scalar↔batch parity test covers `field=\"realised\"` with α=0.10.\n  \n  ## (e) 1.7 dB implementation margin — **NOT LANDED as \"biting\"** (by design; reserve comes from elsewhere)\n  \n  - Constant: `constants_v025.py:44` `IMPLEMENTATION_MARGIN_DB = 1.7` (flagged `VERIFY_SOURCE`).\n  - Use sites: `acm.py:42` (baked into every `threshold_db`, hence `threshold_linear`), `acm.py:109` (`select_mode_margin_off`, U-diagnostic), `acm.py:223` (`U-cap` diagnostic). Only `:42` is on the credit path.\n  - Because the power target is `rate_target_sinr → mode.threshold_linear` (`acm.py:141-155`) and the decode threshold is also a `threshold_linear` (`acm.py:93`), the +1.7 dB appears identically in both. In dB the decode condition reduces to `F ≥ ideal(m_tx) − ideal(m_target)` — **margin-invariant. The 1.7 dB still cancels exactly** in the `a-r`/`a′-r` chain.\n  \n  What actually changed is that a *reserve now exists*, supplied by the q10 quantile, not by the margin. Computed from the shipped code:\n  \n  | n_b | Γ (m_target) | m_target | q10 @30° | m_tx | required F |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | 4 | 4.938 dB | QPSK 3/4 | −2.906 dB | QPSK 1/2 | **−3.030 dB** |\n  | 8 | 11.118 dB | 16APSK 3/4 | −2.906 dB | 8PSK 2/3 | −3.590 dB |\n  | 12 | 16.598 dB | 32APSK 8/9 | −2.906 dB | 32APSK 3/4 | −2.960 dB |\n  \n  Previously this column was **0.000 dB** (F ≥ 1). So the defect's *consequence* is fixed; the margin itself is not. This is exactly what the confirmation doc predicted (\"the v1.9 tenth-percentile rule supplies the decode reserve that the implementation margin does not\"), so the report's §3 phrasing — which implies the cancellation was the thing repaired — is **misleading**: the cancellation is still there and is now harmless.\n  \n  **New artefact worth flagging:** at n_b = 1 and 2 the target mode is QPSK 1/4 / QPSK 2/5 with Γ = −1.442 / +0.608 dB; after the ~3 dB q10 backoff, `select_mode(Γ·q)` returns **`None`** — no transmittable mode at all, so bits are credited **zero** for low-occupancy users whose rate target is nominally feasible. This is a direct mechanical contributor to availability falling 0.791 → 0.453.\n  \n  ## Smoke evidence consistency\n  \n  `probe/ACM-CAUSAL-BEFORE-AFTER-SMOKE-2026-09-09.md:9-10` matches report §3 (`:29-30`) exactly on all eight figures. Derived checks: 240,072,304,316.296 / 12,675.247090 = **18,940,246.4987** (quoted 18,940,246.499 ✓); 71,728,548,992.593 / 12,675.247090 = **5,658,946.8026** (quoted 5,658,946.803 ✓); EE drop **70.1221 %** (quoted 70.122 % ✓). One nit: the smoke doc's \"lowers availability by 0.338138\" — 0.791277 − 0.453138 = 0.338**139**; consistent only if derived from unrounded values.\n  \n  **Identical joules is not merely plausible, it is required by the code, and I confirm it.** Energy is `schedule_energy(... slot.beam_rf_w ...)` (`resolution.py:146-154`, `adapter.py:197-203`) over powers produced solely from nominal gains (traced in (b) §4); `batch.py:483-504` likewise derives PA/circuit/baseband power from `power`, which the ACM branch never touches. `resolution.py:144-145` states the invariant explicitly (\"No branch edits radiation: an unsuccessful attempt continues to interfere and consume exactly the energy already scheduled\"). Bit-identical joules is the correct signature of a credit-semantics-only change. **Caveat:** this holds *because the smoke replayed the same BASE profiles and powers* (doc `:5`). It is a paired diagnostic, not a re-optimised run — under re-selection the arms would pick different coalitions and joules would move. The doc says this; the report §3 does not, and a reader could take 12,675.247090 as an invariant of the corrected engine. It is not.\n  \n  ---\n  \n  ## Verdicts\n  \n  | element | verdict | key evidence |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | (a) three distinct objects, all emitted | **LANDED** (caveat) | `architectures.py:193-195`, `:480-510`; `probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:2990-2998`. `m_target` is `None` for `b`/`a-γ`/`a′-γ`; receipt granularity is census, not per-step row |\n  | (b) `m_tx` causally clean | **LANDED** | `architectures.py:462-480`, `:106-107`, `:430`; `channel.py:303-307`; `batch.py:260,284,398-403`. No realised quantity reachable |\n  | (c) credit = bits(`m_tx`) iff realised ≥ threshold(`m_tx`), else 0 | **LANDED** | `acm.py:86-98`; `resolution.py:126-139`; `batch.py:416-419`. `ACMRate.rate_bps` genie path still exists but is unreachable for ACM |\n  | (d) scalar/batch same rule | **PARTIAL** | Logic agrees; but no test passes `fading_quantile_alpha` to `evaluate_ar_tdm_catalogue`, and the sole parity test `test_stage4d_gate.py:655-685` uses `field=\"nominal\"`, α=None — the corrected branch is untested |\n  | (e) 1.7 dB margin now bites | **NOT LANDED** (by design) | `constants_v025.py:44`; `acm.py:42` (credit path), `:109`, `:223` (diagnostics only). Margin cancels exactly between power target and decode threshold; the ~3 dB reserve comes entirely from the q10 quantile |\n  \n  No files were modified.</result>\n  <usage><subagent_tokens>92766</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>38</tool_uses><duration_ms>295807</duration_ms></usage>\n  </task-notification>"}
