(**a-r TDM, the primary arm**), `ARCH:883-890` (a′-r FDM). `ARCH:553` FixedRF is a constant cap.\n  - `_solve_power` body `ARCH:392` / `ARCH:430`: `targets*(noise + coupling@power)/direct` — only the nominal arrays it was handed.\n  - Batch/hot path: `BATCH:313` and `BATCH:366-374` divide by `direct_nominal` (`BATCH:260`), with `coupling = nominal_cross * active_pair` (`BATCH:300`). The quantile (`BATCH:261-265`) is applied *only* at `BATCH:266-270` (`direct_field`) and `BATCH:403` (`predicted_sinr`).\n  - KAT: `T4H:95-109` asserts `slot.beam_rf_w` identical between `\"nominal\"` and `\"margin\"` radiations.\n  \n  Falsification attempt: no call site of `_solve_power` or of the batch solver receives `Geometry.gains(\"margin\")` (`ARCH:108-120`) — grep of all 5 architectures confirms.\n  \n  ### (2) QUANTILE ONLY ON THE WANTED LINK — **VERDICT: LANDED**\n  \n  - `ARCH:129-134` `Geometry.cross`: `if field == \"margin\": return nominal_cross_gain` — the quantile is structurally unreachable for interference.\n  - `BATCH:288-295`: `field_cross = nominal_cross` unless `field == \"realised\"`; the SINR denominator at `BATCH:383-388` uses `field_cross`, the numerator `power * direct_field` (quantile-scaled only for `margin`).\n  - `ARCH:462-463, 475-482, 509`: `nominal_sinr` from `nominal_direct`/`nominal_coupling`; `margin_predicted_sinr = nominal_sinr * quantile` — one scalar factor on S only.\n  - KAT `T4H:114-117`: `intra_interference_w` and `inter_interference_w` bit-equal between nominal and margin, while `margin_predicted_sinr &lt; nominal_sinr`.\n  \n  ### (3) FULL FADING-PRODUCT QUANTILE — **VERDICT: LANDED**\n  \n  - `CHAN:41-43`: `FADING_QUANTILE_DRAWS = 200_000`, `FADING_QUANTILE_ELEVATION_BIN_DEG = 0.5`, domain `\"V025_FADING_PRODUCT_QUANTILE/v1\"`.\n  - `CHAN:293-300`: product is `rician * 10**(-(shadow_db + scintillation_loss_db(bin))/10)` — all three factors (Rician power `CHAN:292`→`CHAN:182-200`, lognormal shadow `CHAN:289-291`, deterministic scintillation