nstruction (`PROBE:3655-3657`, receipt `PROBE:4070-4074`).\n  - (d) tie-breaks: `PROBE:2424-2454` `_c2_tie_diagnostic` iterates `ARM_PRIMARY_COMPONENTS`, reporting `secondary = \"C2\" if arm != \"DROP_C2\" else \"configuration_id\"` (`PROBE:2452`).\n  - Receipt claim `PROBE:4042-4048` matches the code, including `\"DROP_C2\": \"primary C1_m+C3_m; secondary configuration_id\"`.\n  - KAT `T4H:144-167` exercises all four arms with adversarial factor values.\n  \n  Gaps found by adversarial search:\n  1. **`PROBE:3613` prunes before `PROBE:3633`.** `factors[...][\"C2\"]` is `Fraction()` for every row at pruning time (set to 0 in `_selection_factor_scores`, `PROBE:2241`; only filled by `_attach_stage2_c2` at `PROBE:2420`, called at `PROBE:3633`). So at top-M the secondary key is identically zero and pruning ties fall through to `configuration_id` (`PROBE:2180-2182`). Formula is arm-correct; the secondary is degenerate at stage 1. Benign at M=48, but it is not literally \"the same key\".\n  2. **`PROBE:3704` `changed_full = selections[\"FULL\"].changed_users`** drives `decomposition_rows`→`validation_reserve_s`→`deadline_missed` (`PROBE:3705-3725`), which then forces *every* arm to BASE via `apply_deadline_fallback` (`PROBE:3727`). This is a FULL-arm-derived quantity gating all arms — the one place where a single global quantity acts as a guard. Effect is symmetric (all-or-none), but it is not arm-specific.\n  3. Diagnostics `PROBE:2819` (`rankings[\"FULL\"][0]`) and `PROBE:2837-2841` (`include=(\"C1\",\"C2\",\"C3\")`) are FULL-key-only; labelled as diagnostics, not decision-bearing.\n  \n  ---\n  \n  ### v1.7 (two decompositions; caps)\n  \n  - Separation holds in code: selection view is `field=\"margin\"`, `boundary_indices=(0,)` (`PROBE:3538-3553`); outcome view is the default `field=\"realised\"`, all 48 boundaries (`PROBE:1334,1337`) used by `_committed_set_decomposition` at `PROBE:3767-3782` and `PROBE:678-709`. `matched_anchor_decomposition` (`PROBE:3915-3928`) is built from realised profiles only. Receipt declares the split at `PROBE:4060-4066`.\n  - Interaction labels uncapped: `PROBE:2570-2581` — for `|A|&gt;4` it evaluates `{}`, singletons, joint (|A|+2), so Ψ_A is exact at any size.\n  - Shapley split capped: `PROBE:2579` (`1 &lt; len(changed) &lt;= 4` for the full powerset) and `targets.py:498,510` (`EXACT_SHAPLEY_SMALL_SET` / `NOT_COMPUTED_LARGE_SET`); KAT `T4H:170-194`.\n  - **NOT LANDED:** `V_CA`, the reversal frequency, and the S_UNI-re-anchored decomposition (v1.6 §3, cited verbatim in v1.7 §2) exist nowhere in the repo — grep for `V_CA|collision_avoid|reversal` hits only legacy `.scratch/mone-v010`, `.scratch/pnfe-v09`, `.scratch/joint-c3-v011`. `PROBE:4061` declares `\"F_m ... d_i^m, Psi_A^m and V_CA only\"` as a receipt string for a statistic that is never computed. \"Never mixed\" is currently satisfied by absence.\n  \n  ### v1.8 receipt header\n  \n  `PROBE:4983-5004` carries 6 of 9 items: energy boundary sentence verbatim (`PROBE:186-193` == v1.8 §3), traffic model §5, `\"pa_efficiency_name\": \"saturation efficiency\"` §1 (constants `PA_MAX_EFFICIENCY=0.35`, `PA_SATURATION_POWER_W` at `constants_v025.py:36-37`, law at `energy.py:38`), hardware mapping §2, atomic application §6, causality §7. §8 (`m_target`/`m_tx`/realised reported separately) is implemented — `PROBE:2991-2992`, `PROBE:4233-4255`, sourced from `ARCH:503-509` and `ACM:73-98`. **Absent from the header:** §4 (E₀ non-cancellation statement), §9 (link-closure ledger — exists only as the sibling artefacts `build_stage4h_link_ledger.py` / `LINK-CLOSURE-LEDGER-2026-09-09.md`, not referenced in the receipt), and §7's full verbatim deployability sentence (only an abbreviated `causality_rule`).\n  \n  ### Conformance-test coverage (v1.9 §8) — thin\n  \n  The power/interference invariance KAT (`T4H:95-118`) covers only `AngleTPC_TDM` (a-γ) on the scalar path. There is **no** KAT for the primary `a-r` architecture, **none** for the batch path `evaluate_a