/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:9:5. **Report schema — anti-pattern statistics (round 9D).** The terminal report must contain, per contrast: net collision-avoidance value with both components unclipped; the additive-reversal frequency and whether the coordinator prevents them; escape recall and harmful-acceptance rate stratified by coalition size; top-choice agreement between the learned and exact selectors; the full decision-latency distribution including feature construction, catalogue generation, physics-call count, timeout frequency and fallback-inclusive outcomes; and the four experiments of §C3 reported separately and never interchanged.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:10:6. **Certified comparator.** A budget-limited S_UNI is an operational comparator and is labelled as such; only a S_UNI with a completed-neighbourhood termination certificate supports the "beyond exhaustive unilateral improvement" claim (v1.6 §4). An offline certified reference may be used to diagnose available joint headroom provided its different computational status is stated.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:1:# V025 stages 6–8 contract v1 — source generation, learner, evaluation (controller; sealed 2026-09-08 ≈ 18:45 UTC; supersedes v0; no successor training exists)
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:6:A1. **I_heads** (per user i, per legal action): the completed Q1 and Q2 schemas of §B; observation access = current nominal geometry of user i's candidates, i's history, the previous committed served set excluding i (b⁻₋ᵢ) at decision time; derived features as frozen; model access = none (no joint physics); compute = one forward pass.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:8:A3. **Two distinct references:** a⁰ (the reference proposal for the score decomposition; = the per-user argmax of Q1 + Q2, validated as a profile) and the previous committed association (the reference for handover/Φ/event accounting). Never conflated.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:12:B1. One production builder from tapes; every row carries world/user/action/time/schema/setting/calibration lineage; TRAIN asserted at construction; dependency-allowlist KAT (labels are functions of visible primitives, masks, keyed fading, declared state only).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:13:B2. **Q1 schema** (per action; scales frozen in the spec v1 draft): nominal rate-target SINR margin, required power / cap, mode SE, occupancy excluding focal, beam- and satellite-active bits before focal insertion, off-axis angle, remaining D2 time, remaining visibility time, refresh phase; history: previous served association one-hot, previous served load per candidate, previous beam/satellite activity, previous beam max RF / cap; `missing_incumbent`. No recurrence power, entry-gain ratio or segment age.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:19:C1. **Heads:** Q1, Q2 by pairwise zero-bootstrap regression on typed deterministic aggregate batches (legacy heterogeneous design); the deployed two-head action is the per-user masked argmax of the normalised Q1 + Q2, validated as a jointly legal profile (deterministic repair rule for conflicts, KAT with a jointly infeasible pair). This estimates a supervised surrogate of the declared targets, not a Bellman value; the claim is worded accordingly.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:21:C3. **Arms and estimands (four named experiments, never conflated):** (i) *learned neutral-source experiment* (primary for the C1/C2/C3 claims): FULL, DROP_C1, DROP_C2, DROP_C3 by neutral-source substitution of the named route with all routes retained, updated and deployed; ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL; external BASELINE; claim wording: "informative source training for route x improved pooled EE relative to the specified neutral source training, with the other routes informative and all heads retained"; (ii) *oracle factor-score removal* (physics regime map, stage-4 item 18); (iii) *checkpoint knockout* (secondary: zero the deployed contribution, machinery fixed; measures reliance and exposes hidden score restoration); (iv) *architecture removal* — named, not run.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:22:C4. **Coordination attribution (beyond the source claim):** FULL (S3) > DROP_C3 **and** FULL > the S_UNI-equipped comparator on held-out realised pooled EE, QoS margins met, plus decision-relevant nonadditivity (the selected profile differs from the additive/unilateral optimum at a reported fraction of anchors, including rejected harmful joint moves) — the requirement "g_I ≠ 0" is withdrawn. **Learned value (S3 vs matched S0)** is one predeclared axis: realised closed-loop pooled EE under equal computation budget including timeouts; matching S0 at lower compute is an acceleration claim, reported separately.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:24:C6. **Zero results are allowed and informative:** a zero C3 source marginal ends the positive C3 claim under this scope; an interval excluding the practical margin supports "no practically relevant benefit"; a lower-bound failure alone is inconclusive; neither permits changing features, catalogues, sources or regimes until C3 becomes positive.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:25:C7. **Epochs, checkpoints, seeds:** deterministic aggregate epochs with sealed row counts/order/digests; checkpoints every 100 source epochs with `completed_source_epochs` and batch digests; **12 learner seeds** (§E), each lineage sharing one serialised initialisation and identical source batches per route identity across arms; `learner_seed` and `world_seed` separate everywhere.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:28:D1. **Panel:** 6 arms × 12 learner seeds × 2 worlds per TRAIN date over the ≈ 160 claim dates (≈ 320 worlds per arm-seed; ≈ 30 steps per world), allocation manifest sealed with role-wise date disjointness (claim dates unused by any successor development activity; legacy overlap recorded); no TEST.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:29:D2. **Estimator:** pooled ΣB/ΣE; primary interval = two-way pigeonhole bootstrap over dates × learner seeds with arms paired within resamples and the ratio recomputed per draw (central 95 % percentile); one-way cluster bootstrap and delta-method supplementary; seedwise paired effects reported; δ = +0.5 % relative with the 2.5th-percentile lower bound (v1.4); QoS margins with additive numerators/denominators inside draws (stage-2 decision 6, item 37).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:31:D4. **Multiplicity and claim:** the conditional intersection–union conjunction for `a-r0` is the single primary claim; components are reported with their own intervals but no component-wise discovery is claimed; all other cells exploratory; TRAIN-only wording enforced by the report schema.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:35:Planning alternative Δ* = +2 % relative (both reviewers: a true +1 % is not detectable with ≈ 160 dates under any seed count if the date SD is ≈ 5 %). Variance sensitivities: date SD 3 / 5 / 10 %, seed SD 1 / 2 %. With date SD 5 %, seed SD 1 %, 160 dates, 12 seeds and negligible residual variance, the per-contrast one-sided power at the 2.5 % level is ≈ 0.86 (SE ≈ 0.49 %); the three-contrast conjunction ≈ 0.64 if independent. With 5 seeds it is ≈ 0.70 / 0.34. 12 seeds is the declared design; the date component caps further gains. The crossed-cluster inference test (§G T3) calibrates the actual procedure at 5 and 12 seeds before any real evaluation.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:37:## F. Operational contract (deployability; the benchmark and the operational claim are separate)
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:38:F1. **Benchmark convention:** decision at t from information at t, applied from t (legacy convention, kept for the scientific comparison); TLE nearest-epoch rule labelled retrospective (v1.5 §5). **Operational claim** (if made): a causal-input variant (ephemeris available by decision time, causal forecasts) and an explicit action-effective-time convention.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:39:F2. **Timing budget:** the coordinator's compute budget is 10 s wall on the declared worker count (the rest of the 30.08 s interval reserved for sensing/transport/validation/commit); BASE (a⁰) is computed, validated and repaired **before** the coordinator starts; the runner enforces the timer (cancel), not the solver; a miss executes the validated a⁰; misses are a co-reported QoS field and their B/E enter the endpoint.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:45:T3 **Crossed-cluster inference through the real merger:** synthetic raw receipts with controlled date/seed/world effects for the 3/5/10 % SD scenarios, repeated worlds per cell, unequal energies (pooled ≠ mean EE), identical arms, zero-bit and undefined-denominator cells, injected alternatives, least-favourable conjunction null (one component at the +0.5 % boundary); verify pairing, interval calibration, conjunction power and QoS rejection at 5 and 12 seeds.
